+### Inspect a project's integrity
+
+```bash
+python3 /path/to/agent-toolkit/install.py bootstrap --project /path/to/my-project --check
+```
+
+This read-only check validates the recorded ownership manifest, each managed file's
+recorded content hash, and the managed `AGENTS.md` routing block. It reports intact
+installations with exit status 0; missing or edited managed content, malformed or unsafe
+manifests, and unbootstrapped targets fail with a diagnostic and nonzero status. It does
+not create missing targets, write bytecode, or update project files or the manifest.
+Instructions outside the managed block and extra unowned files are ignored and preserved.
+
+`bootstrap --check` checks the installed record, not available upgrades: changes to the
+current toolkit source alone do not cause drift. Use `bootstrap --update --dry-run` to
+preview available changes, or `install.py check` to validate the current toolkit package.
+`--check` cannot be combined with `--update`, `--dry-run`, `--skill`, `--all`, or `--target`.
+The manifest is an ownership record, not a signed guarantee against coordinated edits to
+both the record and managed content.
+
